---
import DocsPage from "../../layouts/DocsPage.astro"

export const prerender = true
---

<DocsPage id="follow">

          <p>
            Watch the agent type. With Follow mode on, the editor opens whatever file the agent is editing, scrolls to
            the lines it changed, tints them in that agent's colour, and places a labelled caret at the end of the
            edit. Every edit is attributed to the agent that made it, so a session with several agents reads like a
            shared document with named cursors.
          </p>
          <dl class="doc-rows">
            <div><dt>Turn it off when you are typing</dt><dd>The eye button in the Codespace toolbar, or Settings → General → "Follow the agent in the editor". Off, the agent's edits to the file you have open are still highlighted; other files stay closed until you open them.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>What it never does</dt><dd>Your own saves, build output, and formatter runs do not move the editor. Only edits published by an agent do.</dd></div>
          </dl>
</DocsPage>
